---
/**
 * Root redirect (spec 5: root redirect).
 *
 * `/` -> `/es/` (302). The middleware also handles this, but a real root route
 * is required by Astro's `i18n.routing.prefixDefaultLocale: true` config so the
 * default locale is never served unprefixed. This page satisfies that
 * requirement and keeps the redirect working even if middleware ordering
 * changes.
 */
// The locale is a LITERAL here, not `DEFAULT_LANG`, and that is forced rather than
// chosen: `astro check` does not analyse the contents of a top-level `return` in
// frontmatter, so ANY identifier referenced only inside it reports ts(6133)
// "declared but its value is never read" — the import itself, or a const holding
// the derived path. Both were tried; both fail.
//
// The coupling this literal loses is restored as a test, not a comment:
// `src/lib/i18n.test.ts` reads this file and asserts the path matches DEFAULT_LANG,
// so changing the default locale fails the suite instead of silently pointing the
// site root at a locale that is no longer the default.
return Astro.redirect('/es/', 302);
---
